cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PHL-DAM: staged empirical investigation of a slot-memory sequence architecture"
message: "If you use this work, cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Liam
    family-names: Pattiata
    email: liampattiata@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  A preregistered, staged investigation of PHL-DAM, a recurrent sequence model
  combining a multi-timescale context state with a bank of eight explicit
  key-value memory slots addressed by content. Includes parameter-matched
  comparisons against a causal Transformer, diagonal and selective state-space
  models, and an NTM/DNC-style differentiable memory; an attribution study that
  rejected the architecture's temporal-lease mechanism; a diagnosed and fixed
  gradient instability; and a write-pressure ladder locating where the
  controller stops learning.
keywords:
  - associative recall
  - memory-augmented neural networks
  - sequence models
  - continual learning
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
date-released: 2026-08-29
